---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import NetWorthCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/NetWorthCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="net-worth-calculator">
  <NetWorthCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the net worth calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      Net worth is <code>total assets − total debts</code>. The debt-to-asset ratio is <code>debts ÷ assets</code>.
      Liquid net worth counts only cash and investments, minus credit card balances, as a measure of money you could
      reach quickly.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      With 15,000 in cash, 40,000 in investments, 85,000 in retirement accounts, a 350,000 home, 20,000 of vehicles and
      5,000 of other assets, you own 515,000. A 260,000 mortgage, 12,000 car loan, 18,000 of student loans and 3,000 on
      cards come to 293,000 of debt. Net worth is 222,000 and the debt-to-asset ratio is 56.9%.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      Use what each asset would sell for today and the payoff amount of each debt. Retirement balances are before the
      tax due on withdrawal. Check your net worth once or twice a year; the change matters more than one figure.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
